lesson: 163
title: Moving towards each other and moving apart
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When two travellers move towards each other, the gap between them shrinks by both their speeds together every hour.
explain: Towns 450 km apart, cars at 70 and 80 km an hour: together they close 70 + 80 = 150 km an hour, so they meet after 450 / 150 = 3 hours.
explain: When they start at one place and go in opposite directions, the gap grows by the sum of the speeds in the same way.
vars: a=name b=name u=40..90 v=40..90 t=2..6
need: (u + v) * t <= 1000
answer: t
exercise: Two towns are {(u+v)*t} km apart. Two cars leave them at the same time and drive towards each other, one at {u} km an hour and the other at {v} km an hour. After how many hours do they meet?
exercise: A train leaves city A for city B at {u} km an hour. At the same moment another train leaves B for A at {v} km an hour. The cities are {(u+v)*t} km apart. In how many hours do the trains meet?
exercise: Two buses leave the same station at the same time and drive in opposite directions at {u} km an hour and {v} km an hour. After how many hours are they {(u+v)*t} km apart?
exercise: {a} and {b} live {(u+v)*t} metres apart. They walk towards each other, {a} at {u} metres a minute and {b} at {v} metres a minute. How many minutes pass before they meet?
exercise: Two children start back to back on one bridge and walk away from each other, one at {u} metres a minute and the other at {v} metres a minute. In how many minutes will {(u+v)*t} metres be between them?
exercise: Two lorries {(u+v)*t} km apart drive towards each other. One goes {u} km an hour, the other {v} km an hour. How long, in hours, until they meet?
test: How many hours will it take two ships to meet if they sail towards each other from ports {(u+v)*t} km apart, at {u} and {v} km an hour?
test: {a} walks {u} metres each minute and {b} walks {v} metres each minute. They set off at the same time from the two ends of a {(u+v)*t}-metre path, each heading for the other. When do they meet, in minutes?
test: From the same crossroads a car goes north at {u} km an hour and a van goes south at {v} km an hour. How many hours later is the distance between them {(u+v)*t} km?
test: The road between two villages is {(u+v)*t} km. Two vans set out from the villages at the same time, one at {u} km an hour, the other at {v} km an hour, and drive until they pass each other. For how many hours did they drive?
exercise: Two cyclists start at the same moment from the two ends of a trail in Oregon that is {(u+v)*t} km long and ride towards each other at {u} km and {v} km an hour. After how many hours do they meet?
exercise: How many hours does it take two trains {(u+v)*t} km apart to meet if they set off together towards each other, one at {u} km per hour and the other at {v} km per hour?
exercise: {a} and {b} drive towards each other along one road in Canada, starting at the same time {(u+v)*t} km apart. {a} drives at {u} km an hour and {b} at {v} km an hour. In how many hours do they meet?
exercise: Two boats leave one pier together and sail in opposite directions, one at {u} km an hour and the other at {v} km an hour. After how many hours will they be {(u+v)*t} km apart?
exercise: Two runners stand back to back in a park in London and run in opposite directions, at {u} and {v} metres a minute. How many minutes pass until they are {(u+v)*t} metres apart?
exercise: {a} and {b} are {(u+v)*t} metres apart on a beach in Queensland. They walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres per minute. After how many minutes do they meet?
exercise: The distance between two farms in Iowa is {(u+v)*t} km. Two trucks set off from the farms at the same time towards each other, at {v} km and {u} km an hour. How many hours pass before they meet?
exercise: Each hour a car covers {u} km and a van covers {v} km. They start at the same time from two towns {(u+v)*t} km apart and head towards each other. After how many hours do they meet?
test: Two coaches leave two towns in Ireland that are {(u+v)*t} km apart at the same time and drive towards each other at {u} and {v} km an hour. How many hours go by until they pass each other?
test: Find the time, in hours, after which two cars leaving the same petrol station in opposite directions at {u} km an hour and {v} km an hour are {(u+v)*t} km apart.
test: {a} cycles {u} metres a minute and {b} cycles {v} metres a minute. They start from the two ends of a track in Auckland that is {(u+v)*t} metres long, riding towards each other. In how many minutes do they meet?
test: A gap of {(u+v)*t} km separates two ships on a lake in Canada. They steam towards each other at {u} and {v} km an hour. How long, in hours, is it before they meet?
test: Two friends say goodbye at a gate in Edinburgh and walk off in opposite directions at {u} and {v} metres a minute. After how many minutes is the distance between them {(u+v)*t} metres?
test: How many minutes pass before {a} and {b} meet if they set off at the same time, {(u+v)*t} metres apart, and run towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute?
