exercise: {a} and {b} live {(u+v)*t} km apart. After their grandmother was laid to rest, they set off towards each other to share out her old photos, {a} driving at {u} km an hour and {b} at {v} km an hour. In how many hours do they meet?
exercise: {a}'s old banger gave up the ghost, so {a.he} gets the coach at {u} km an hour while dad drives out to meet {a.him} at {v}. they're {(u+v)*t} km apart. how many hours till they meet, for crying out loud
test: The bus company said one of its buses was "temporarily out of service" — it had broken down for good. So two other buses, {(u+v)*t} km apart, drive towards each other at {v} and {u} km an hour to swap passengers. When do they meet, in hours?
exam: It is given that two towns are situated {(u+v)*t} km apart, and that two cars depart from them simultaneously, travelling towards each other at {u} km per hour and {v} km per hour respectively. Determine the number of hours elapsing before the cars meet.
exam: Whereas a train departs city A for city B at {u} km per hour, and another train simultaneously departs city B for city A at {v} km per hour, the distance between the cities being {(u+v)*t} km, ascertain the time in hours until the trains meet.
exam: Two motorcars depart simultaneously from the same point and travel in opposite directions at {u} km per hour and {v} km per hour respectively. Ascertain after how many hours the distance between them shall amount to {(u+v)*t} km.
exam: Two coaches set out at the same moment from two cities {(u+v)*t} km apart and proceed towards each other along the same road, the one at {u} km per hour and the other at {v} km per hour. State the number of hours that shall elapse prior to their meeting.
